# REGRESSION (was todo/t0840): the HANDLE-TYPE axis — `Weak[T]`.
# `Weak__T` is the same `Gorget<Family>*` pointer typedef as `Shared__T`, so a
# BOUND `Weak` in a `Vector` carried the identical defect: pre-fix this built
# and then died (rc 135 / 139 depending on lane) with
# `gorget_array_push(__v13, __v15)` storing the handle value under
# `typedef GorgetShared* Weak__int64_t`.
#
# ⚠ An UNBOUND `Vector[Weak[int]]` — declared, never fed from a `downgrade()` —
# was reported as a separate missing-typedef class while this net was being
# built. It does NOT reproduce: `Vector[Weak[int]] all = []` with `len()`,
# `get(0)` and a struct-field root all build and run clean on C and LLVM at
# HEAD, so there is nothing to pin and nothing filed.
#
# ⚠ SANITIZER NOTE: this cell is value-lane green but NOT ASan-clean, for a
# PRE-EXISTING and ALREADY-FILED reason it does not introduce: **`todo/t0620`**,
# whose text matches what this cell measures byte for byte — *"LEAKS 40 bytes
# under LSan (the 32-byte Shared control block + 8-byte value) — the match-bound
# `sh` ... is never drop-registered"*. Regenerated here:
# `SUMMARY: AddressSanitizer: 40 byte(s) leaked in 2 allocation(s)`.
#
# t0620 also records the isolation this cell independently reproduces: the Weak
# CONSUMING position ALONE is ASan-clean, and only the `upgrade()`-result
# binding leaks. So the marshalling half this cell pins is sound, and the leak
# is `t0620`'s — which is why this cell has no ASan twin while its
# ownership-sensitive siblings do. The robustness map carries the same defect as
# a baselined row (`sh_weak_clone_upgrade`, `asan = SANITIZE-FAIL`, note
# *"prints the RIGHT answer"*).
#
# CELL: container=Vector · handle=Weak · payload=int · producing-arm=push ·
#       read=`.get(i).unwrap().upgrade()`.

void main():
    Shared[int] s = Shared[int](9)
    Weak[int] w = s.downgrade()
    Vector[Weak[int]] all = []
    all.push(w.clone())
    all.push(w.clone())
    print(f"{all.len()}")
    match all.get(0).unwrap().upgrade():
        case Some(v):
            print(f"{v.get()}")
        else:
            print("gone")
